# shell-smoke

The named level-1 acceptance application: portable, allocation-free, and
driven entirely by declared static arrays. It installs the standard level-1
pack plus one custom handler and one installed script, then runs a fixed
boundary script covering assignment, a conditional, a loop, checked
arithmetic, a function with a positional argument, command substitution, a
custom native handler, an installed script, and yield, and compares the
output byte for byte.

It uses mm.shell directly with memory sinks and has no dependency on mm.mcu,
mm.stdio, filesystem, or platform providers. A capacity failure exits with 64
plus the StorageClass ordinal, so a run names the array to grow.
docs/modules-shell.mdy records the profile and the measured requirement.
